# Profle of English Learner Students in U.S. Public Schools during the 2020-21 School Year. 2020-21 Civil Rights Data Collection. Data Snapshot

**Authors:** 

## Abstract
The Civil Rights Data Collection (CRDC) is a mandatory survey of all public schools and school districts in the 50 states, Washington, D.C., and the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico. It gathers information about student access to educational programs, activities, staff, and school climate factors from public schools serving students in preschool through 12th grade. This Data Snapshot is profile English Learner (EL) students in U.S. public schools during the 2020-2021 school year.

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=ED650587

